><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20250515132800+10'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20250515132802+10'00'" name="f73250a8-3248-4b6a-ad74-5e806ca4ea10" page="5" coords="312.828278,703.799072,547.929260,703.799072,312.828278,692.182800,547.929260,692.182800,302.850739,692.347046,547.910767,692.347046,302.850739,680.730774,547.910767,680.730774,302.850739,680.895020,548.001770,680.895020,302.850739,669.278748,548.001770,669.278748,302.850739,669.442993,547.970947,669.442993,302.850739,657.826721,547.970947,657.826721,302.850739,657.934204,547.911194,657.934204,302.850739,646.317932,547.911194,646.317932,302.850739,646.482178,547.926575,646.482178,302.850739,634.865906,547.926575,634.865906,302.850739,635.030151,548.016907,635.030151,302.850739,623.413879,548.016907,623.413879,302.850739,623.578125,547.913330,623.578125,302.850739,611.961853,547.913330,611.961853,302.850739,612.126099,548.031799,612.126099,302.850739,600.509827,548.031799,600.509827,302.850739,600.674072,547.909363,600.674072,302.850739,589.057800,547.909363,589.057800,302.850739,589.222046,547.911011,589.222046,302.850739,577.605774,547.911011,577.605774,302.850739,577.770020,548.017700,577.770020,302.850739,566.153748,548.017700,566.153748,302.850739,566.317993,547.924194,566.317993,302.850739,554.701721,547.924194,554.701721,302.850739,554.865967,547.929443,554.865967,302.850739,543.249695,547.929443,543.249695,302.850739,543.413940,548.035706,543.413940,302.850739,531.797668,548.035706,531.797668,302.850739,531.905151,395.880859,531.905151,302.850739,520.288879,395.880859,520.288879" rect="302.487732,519.925903,548.398682,704.162109" subject="Comment on Text" title="alexd"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-13.3pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Supporting children to participate in physical activity and&#xD;sport is important for their health and well-being, and for society.&#xD;Financial incentives can effectively increase children's participation;&#xD;however, their effectiveness appears to be impacted&#xD;by their design, value, and the mechanismunderpinning the incentive.&#xD;Direct incentives increase intrinsic motivation and&#xD;have better accessibility, as they can make sport affordable to&#xD;people who otherwise couldn't afford it, whereas indirect incentives&#xD;increase extrinsic motivation and may be less accessible.&#xD;Financial incentives are more likely to be effective if they offer&#xD;a direct incentive, are of higher value, and support a wide variety&#xD;of activities, so that young people have the freedom to&#xD;choose what they participate in. In designing and implementing&#xD;a financial incentive, it is important to consider equity of access,&#xD;so that the uptake of the financial incentives does not widen&#xD;participation inequities.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="5" rect="584.956970,611.799072,768.956970,703.799072"
/></highlight
